<title>USA: U.N. okays another Iraqi oil contract, total at 21.</title>
<headline>U.N. okays another Iraqi oil contract, total at 21.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.N. overseers have approved another Iraqi oil contract under the oil-for-food plan, raising the total of contracts approved to 21, according to a U.N. spokesman Monday.</p>
<p>No further details on the contract were provided by the U.N. Industry sources believe the total amount of oil contracted for lifting is rapidly approaching the limit permitted under the deal.</p>
<p>The plan went into effect December 10, and allows Iraq to sell $2 billion worth of crude oil over six months to buy food, medicine and other goods for its people suffering from trade sanctions imposed in August 1990.</p>
<p>--Patrick Connole, +1 212 859 1828</p>
</text>
